# Deny everything, then allow back only what the Dockerfile actually COPYs.
#
# An allowlist rather than a denylist: the build context is uploaded to the
# remote builder on EVERY deploy, and a denylist silently regrows (this repo
# reached 4.4 GB / 48k files — .worktrees/ 3.1 GB, dashboard/ 1.1 GB,
# .fastembed_cache/ 134 MB — none of which the image uses). If a future
# Dockerfile COPY adds a path, the build fails loudly with a missing file
# instead of quietly re-inflating every deploy.
*

# Builder stage (Dockerfile lines 12-17, 32-40)
!Cargo.toml
!Cargo.lock
!crates/
!config/
!migrations/
!docs/
docs/*
!docs/openapi.json

# Artifacts that can appear inside the allowed paths
**/target/
**/*.rs.bk
**/.DS_Store
